    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0733" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 France/682: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in France (Armour)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-07T12:00:00-04:00">June 7,
                            1932—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>213. British and Italian [representatives?] signed Hoover year debt postponement agreement Saturday.<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d404-f1"/> Treasury feels that it must within a very short time
                    request French payment due June 15th unless French agreement can be completed at
                    once.</p>
                <p>Department assumes you are pressing this matter in every feasible manner. Please
                    report by wire.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d404-f1" n="43" xml:id="d404-f1-content">
